= Lesson 5.1: Introduction to Communication Protocols

== The OSI Reference Model
#grid(
  columns: (2fr, 3fr),
  gutter: 2em,
  [#align(center, image("../images/50/gp_OSI.png", width: 100%))],
  [
    The Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model standardizes the communication functions of a telecommunication or computing system into seven distinct abstraction layers. 
    
    In the context of microcontrollers and hardware-level digital communication, our focus is predominantly on the *Physical Layer* and the *Data Link Layer*.
    - Layer 1 dictates the electrical and physical specifications of the data connection (e.g., voltage levels, transmission mediums, line impedance, and bit-level timing).
    - Layer 2 handles node-to-node data transfer, framing, and basic error detection.
  ]
)

#v(0.4cm)

#grid(
  columns: (1fr, 1fr),
