  [== Control and Status Registers
    
  #align(top, image("../images/50/UxSTA.png", width: 100%))
  
  `UxSTA`: UART Status and Control Register. It contains the flags that monitor hardware events and configure buffer interactions.
  - *`UTXISEL`*: Defines the condition that triggers the transmission interrupt flag.
  - *`URXISEL`*: Defines the condition that triggers the reception interrupt flag.
  - *`UTXEN`*: Transmit Enable bit. Must be set *after* the UART is enabled.
  - *`TRMT`*: Transmit Shift Register Empty bit (Read-only). `1` means transmission is fully complete (TSR and FIFO are empty).
  - *`URXDA`*: Receive Buffer Data Available bit. `1` means at least one unread character is in the RX FIFO.
  - *`OERR`*: Receive Buffer Overrun Error Status bit.

  === Managing Overrun Errors (OERR)
  An overrun occurs when the 4-level RX FIFO is full and a 5th character is completely received into the Receive Shift Register (RSR). When `OERR = 1`, the hardware strictly blocks any further incoming bytes to protect existing data. 
  
  *Recovery protocol:* The user must clear the error in software (`UxSTAbits.OERR = 0`). It is possible to either:
  1. Read out the existing valid bytes from `UxRXREG` to rescue them, then clear `OERR`.
  2. Clear `OERR` immediately (flushing the buffer and losing unread data).],

  [== Mode Registers
    
  #align(top, image("../images/50/UxMODE.png", width: 100%))
  
  `UxMODE`: UARTx Mode Register. Configures the fundamental protocol parameters.
  - *`UARTEN`*: UART Enable bit. Powers up the peripheral.
  - *`PDSEL`*: Parity and Data Selection bits (e.g., 8-bit no parity, 8-bit even parity, 9-bit data).
  - *`STSEL`*: Stop Bit Selection (1 or 2 stop bits).
  - *`BRGH`*: High Baud Rate Enable bit. Modifies the BRG multiplier (4x or 16x).

  #blueBox([*Core Data and Timing Registers*\ 
  - `UxRXREG`: The memory-mapped register to read received characters (pulls from the RX FIFO).
  - `UxTXREG`: The memory-mapped register to queue characters for transmission (pushes to the TX FIFO).
  - `UxBRG`: The 16-bit Baud Rate Generator register.
  
  *Baud Rate Calculation:*
